"""Mutations of part 7c's actors (src/game/explosive_place.*, ladder.*, pike.*, fowl_generator.* and the
box radius of src/game/frame_box_volume.h) for ../mutfast.py with the actors build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_world.py --models DIR --build build_item.bat --check check_item.py

Each should make check_item.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Left out as equivalent: the
explosive countdown's clamps (a time of 0 ends at 0 either way); LengthOf's / NormalizeBy's near-1
tests (only a square of exactly 1 is within 1e-8 of 1, and its root is 1); summing orders and
x * (1 / s) against x / s (rounding only, no limit met exactly: the ladder's dots, levels, axis and
speed, the pike's step, the fowl generator's distance); the y parts (the ladder's direction is
level, so y never counts: its dot's y, a facing's y kept, NormalizeBy's y scale and sign); the
world matrices' w column and m[3][3] (0 and 1: the ladder's ends' w and direction's w, the
matrix rows' 4th column, the birds' sound's w); the ladder's top volume nulled before it is made;
a NaN height at its top (a NaN height is always nearer the bottom); the pike's SetFrame(null)
(the base's checks too) and its angle kept before the wait (the wait leaves it); the fowl
generator's time cleared before Start (Start clears it: LoadGame clears flown first), a second
Start from the humans' loop (flown by then) and the properties' empty-chunk test (Descend fails
there too).

Results (2026-10-27): the first run caught 647 of 749; 31 survivors were equivalent and one
mutation did not compile (all dropped, above); 70 needed new cases (exact limits and NaNs in
CanUse, tiny vectors in its normalisation, blocked waits ending at 1 and below 0, arrival exactly
at an end, slot 0 loops, untouched state on Hit / slot 0x20, Place in every state and of another
item type, frame failures mid-square, a flock of exactly 3, slot 32 and gaps in the actor list,
countdowns ending at 0). The full rerun of 717: all but a Start without a client side (new case)
and one mutation that did not compile (fixed); those two: caught. All 717 caught (16 of them by a
crash)."""
